-- Retired: laplace_eff_mu(subject, type, object) -> bigint.
-- A convenience wrapper that looked up one consensus row and returned
-- eff_mu(rating, rd). It was marked `STABLE SET search_path`, and the SET clause
-- blocks SQL inlining — so in a WHERE/ORDER BY it would have run per-row and could
-- not match the (rating - 2*rd) expression indexes that every other eff_mu caller
-- relies on. It had zero callers tree-wide (readers open-code eff_mu(c.rating, c.rd)
-- against the consensus row they already hold), so it was dead code that also
-- violated the eff_mu inlining law. On the UPGRADE path the old catalog row would
-- linger; a fresh CREATE EXTENSION never had it. This DROP makes the two match.
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS laplace_eff_mu(bytea, bytea, bytea);
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS laplace.laplace_eff_mu(bytea, bytea, bytea);
